id: pm-starter-cancellation-consumer
title: Resume budgeted paginated reads safely after cancellation
description: "Compose host output sessions and producer/output continuations in a read-only extension recipe; caller-owned checkpoints, typed SDK and CLI, bounded agent receipts."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: audit-1025,cancellation,pagination
created_at: "2026-10-29T02:13:45.874Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T14:25:42.007Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T14:25:38.275Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T03:01:45.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Canceling after page two resumes after the last admitted row without duplicates; Wrong-snapshot cursors produce typed recovery; No source tracker writes are required
release: 2026.10.29
resolution: "Delivered by PR #171 (c859b8c): Resume budgeted paginated reads safely after cancellation"
expected_result: Canceling after page two resumes after the last admitted row without duplicates; Wrong-snapshot cursors produce typed recovery; No source tracker writes are required
actual_result: "PR #171 merged at 2026-10-29T03:01:45Z as c859b8c; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T02:13:50.260Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: pinned pm-cli 2026.10.25 SDK already exposes PmClient.list, outputSession/read_session.next_state, outputCursor, after, producer continuation discriminators and typed native refusals. Current public host is 2026.10.28. pm-rust owns native read sessions (src/read_session.rs); pm-ts-starter owns generated type-control-flow templates. Existing pm-starter labs, failure-first recovery and task baselines do not provide a cancellation/checkpoint consumer. No matching open package PR or issue found. This feature composes those host contracts without another cursor encoder, snapshot store or source mutations. Caller-carried checkpoints avoid shared mutable package state; no transaction isolation is claimed (pm-cli#1620)."
  "2026-10-29T02:20:14.417Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: consumePaginated and starter consume use injected PmClient.list only. Host-owned outputSession accounting is carried as scalar budget state; ID-only pages require no previous full-fact retention. Native producer after/outputCursor are preserved verbatim, including mixed continuation routing. Admission is page-atomic; an aborted in-flight page is charged but not admitted. Checkpoints are caller-owned values, never shared package files: external delivery and checkpoint persistence require a caller journal/lease and are not claimed exactly once. Producer cursors require a stable source; output cursors fail closed on host snapshot mismatch. Tests use non-git native trackers, output fault injection after genuine SDK reads, and a 500-sequence state/read-back model."
  "2026-10-29T02:33:52.009Z",codex-agent,"Public main tracker validation at afccd8575f7473955a83681a379a345dd174ccc6: 84 items; 174 authoritative files; 1324757 source bytes. Read-only non-git copy: canceled after 2 producer pages (14 admitted), resumed 70, completed in 12 total pages with 84 unique IDs and 7960 host-estimated tokens. Output continuation mode completed in 3 pages with 4058 host-estimated tokens. Canceled/final JSON receipts measured 524/392 bytes. SDK read-back state identical and authoritative byte hashes unchanged (0 changes). Existing files were made read-only; only host-derived runtime/lock caches could be created. Additional overlap check: current open sibling PRs in pm-ts-starter and pm-rust contain no duplicate cancellation consumer."
  "2026-10-29T02:35:47.708Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable non-git copy: replacing native producer cursor advancement with the prior checkpoint cursor makes the page-two cancellation regression fail (0 passed, 1 failed). Original worktree untouched; fixed code rerun passes. Targeted native consumer suite: 8 passed; measured paginated-consumer.ts coverage 100% lines, 100% branches, 100% functions, unchanged thresholds. SDK floor and smoke suite: 13 passed. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and diff whitespace checks pass. Tiny native session envelopes expose an upstream missing-code UX gap, tracked separately as pm-starter-session-refusal-code; no native prose is parsed or fictitious code inferred."
  "2026-10-29T02:40:10.638Z",codex-agent,"All five packed acceptance routes passed against host 2026.10.28: npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx and project-local. Each admitted 4 rows then resumed 1; JSON/TOON measured 610/490 bytes. Captured artifact SHA256 041baa4784d9cb035fcc100184366cf6238a5d915003cbc5852d1c4a6ffb7d8a; digest checked before every route and after acceptance. Artifact stays ignored locally. A linked run of all 9 focused tests hit the default 120-second runner timeout after the first 8 tests passed under host load; retained the refusal and raised only that linked command timeout to 600 seconds for a complete rerun, without changing test or coverage thresholds. The package includes no new import/export/sync write path; seeded-model tests compare read-back native state, not handwritten normalization."
  "2026-10-29T02:42:58.307Z",codex-agent,"Complete linked test rerun: node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-starter-cancellation-consumer --run --progress --timeout 600 passed 9 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped in 100.5 seconds. Native pm test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains the measured result without enabling unrelated policy. Persisting timeout_seconds metadata was refused by the host's item-format minimum-version guard; no formats or history were rewritten, and the per-run timeout override succeeded. Additional model inputs round-trip historical checkpoints through compact/pretty JSON with surrounding whitespace and CRLF variants. Final CI is the required npm plus Bun release gate on Node 22 and 26; pending until the final commit is pushed. Producer enumeration requires a stable source; caller-owned journals are required for durable external delivery."
  "2026-10-29T02:45:11.576Z",codex-agent,"Final local checks: linked focused suite 9 passed; expanded 500-sequence whitespace/CRLF replay test rerun 1 passed; SDK-floor/smoke suite 13 passed; new consumer module measured 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions. Build, production/test typecheck, docstring lint (14 files, 113 declarations), changelog full/check and diff checks pass. Strict pm health passes with isolated HOME and credential-free child environment; an ambient extension cache version mismatch is absent in that fresh context. Claim released; both pm items remain open for orchestrator verification. No full local suites were run; CI npm/Bun release gates on the final head remain the full-gate authority."
